  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2ebd63107ccd4720bc00647b5eb2bc0a",
      "statement": "The shared connect lifecycle: connectAccount returns a URL embedding a cryptographic nonce to prevent replay, backed by a UserAccount DO that stores the callback; GitHub's implementation sets a 1-hour alarm at setCallback and its alarm() deletes the account if no access token ever arrived, matching the contract's advice that the DO self-destruct when the flow is never completed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1045-L1062",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10153c2528d122a09030c8edfc93fe9ed3fb156a20449d147853d2038dafa298:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1165-L1169",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b74f93561ecc447545bdb7bf4176ef328a55b92dd63b4013810441160d45948:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L449-L480",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb0096947919d9296f52b854e8af710efc77fb5731524f515210ce33fb872ade:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_681f9e58c9a3445189d7c6a8bc371418",
      "statement": "The OAuth callback handshake is two-stage: beginOAuthFlow verifies the initiation nonce with a constant-time comparison, mints a fresh oauth-stage nonce, and returns the authorize parameters; acceptAuthCode verifies that second nonce, deletes it (single use), exchanges the code with the client credentials, and stores accessToken + granted scopes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1074-L1113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca5c64f65103414df58b7d048029a8f8d055ec54f19f31153648bceaaf68d37b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a727070349cc497a8019b6f06c0add14",
      "statement": "Completion branches by mode: a connect flow calls callback.complete(GatekeeperUserImpl) and deletes the freshly stored token if complete() throws (no grant outlives a failed registration); a reconnect calls credentialsRestored(); an ephemeral (sign-in) grant self-destructs via a 2-minute alarm WITHOUT calling the provider's revoke endpoint, because revoking could invalidate the user's other grants for the same OAuth app.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1115-L1134",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0282d5a9941d95c5c560cc553322818b5203c26c47a8d81b87659b28cd9329d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc3ec87906c24298a5276959fba62785",
      "statement": "Credential expiry is proactive or reactive: complete() may carry an expiresAt for proactive UI, otherwise the gatekeeper calls credentialsExpired() when refresh/authorization fails — GitHub notifies exactly once (guarded by an expiredNotified flag) when an API call hits an auth error, and the failing call is surfaced to the caller as 'credentials have expired, please reconnect'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-github/src/github.ts#L1153-L1163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7bdd9def30fabbb1b634287253a3ccb7bb018e81696cda63cc1ff70670dfae0:"
