    {
      "id": "claim_0856a0ba67c94ef5b6e4daa1588d5c52",
      "statement": "GitHub simulates unapproved writes so agents keep working: actions are staged with provisional resource ids (~<n>), created resources resolve to real ids at apply time, dependent actions are rejected along with the rejection of their provisional target, and markdown references like #~12 are rewritten to real issue numbers when the action is applied — an example of the mutate-the-cache simulation approach the write-gatekeeper skill documents.",
