    {
      "id": "claim_cb30a180d7284299a489424681404a13",
      "statement": "Observer verification uses the 'non-standard method on the verifier' pattern: the overseer passes a GatekeeperUserVerifier only back to the vendor that minted it, and the vendor extends it with its own check — GitHub's GitHubVerifier.hasRepoAccess queries with the OBSERVER's own token, treating a 404 on GET /repos/{owner}/{repo} as no access (GitHub returns 404, not 403, for invisible repos).",
